    "q-341788": {
      "dom_id": "step-q341788",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi }{3}x)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi }{3}x)\n$$\n\nLet $F(x)=4{x}^{2}-6x+3$ for $x\\in [-3,3).$ The Fourier series of the $6$-periodic extension $f(x)$ of $F(x)$ is shown above. Find the exact value of ${a}_{0}.$\n\n${a}_{0}=$ {{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "For the Fourier series of a $2L$-periodic function, the constant term is given by\n\n$$\n{a}_{0}=\\frac{1}{L}{\\int }_{-L}^{L}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $L=3$ and $f(x)=4{x}^{2}-6x+3$ for $x\\in [-3,3).$ So, substituting into the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{0} & =\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{-3}^{3}(4{x}^{2}-6x+3)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{[\\frac{4}{3}{x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}+3x]}_{-3}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}((\\frac{4}{3}\\cdot {3}^{3}-3\\cdot {3}^{2}+3\\cdot 3)-(\\frac{4}{3}\\cdot (-3)^{3}-3\\cdot (-3)^{2}+3\\cdot (-3))) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(18-(-72)) \\\\  & =30.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
