    "q-341808": {
      "dom_id": "step-q341808",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi }{9}x)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi }{9}x)\n$$\n\nLet $F(x)=3x+\\frac{1}{2}$ for $x\\in [-9,9).$ The Fourier series of the $18$-periodic extension $f(x)$ of $F(x)$ is shown above. Find the exact value of ${a}_{0}.$\n\n${a}_{0}=$ {{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "For the Fourier series of a $2L$-periodic function, the constant term is given by\n\n$$\n{a}_{0}=\\frac{1}{L}{\\int }_{-L}^{L}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $L=9$ and $f(x)=3x+\\frac{1}{2}$ for $x\\in [-9,9).$ So, substituting into the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{0} & =\\frac{1}{9}{\\int }_{-9}^{9}(3x+\\frac{1}{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}{[\\frac{3}{2}{x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{2}x]}_{-9}^{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}((\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot {9}^{2}+\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 9)-(\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot (-9)^{2}+\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (-9))) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}(126-117) \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
