    "q-341815": {
      "dom_id": "step-q341815",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi }{3}x)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi }{3}x)\n$$\n\nThe Fourier series of the $6$-periodic extension $f(x)$ of the function \n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}1, & x\\in [0,3) \\\\ -4, & x\\in [-3,0)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nis shown above. Find the exact value of ${a}_{2}.$\n\n${a}_{2}=$ {{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "For the Fourier series of a $2L$-periodic function, the cosine coefficients are given by\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}=\\frac{1}{L}{\\int }_{-L}^{L}f(x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi }{L}x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $L=3.$ Also, $f(x)=1$ for $x\\in [0,3)$ and $f(x)=-4$ for $x\\in [-3,0).$ So, substituting into the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{-3}^{3}f(x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{2\\pi }{3}x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{-3}^{0}(-4)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{2\\pi }{3}x)\\,\\text{d}x+\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{2\\pi }{3}x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{3}\\cdot \\frac{3}{2\\pi }{[\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{2\\pi }{3}x)]}_{-3}^{0}+\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot \\frac{3}{2\\pi }{[\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{2\\pi }{3}x)]}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{\\pi }(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-2\\pi ))+\\frac{1}{2\\pi }(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\pi )-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
